  "not_simulated": [
    { "what": "light", "why": "The engine reports current, not luminous intensity. The drawing scales current by 10 mA, so the glow is 1 at 10 mA and blooms above that. The candela at that current is not modeled. The forward curve is fitted from 2 mA to 20 mA as its source names. Below 2 mA and above 20 mA the current is that curve extended. A threshold at 1 mA would sit outside the fit. Luminous intensity versus forward current is drawn as a straight line from 0 mA, so the extended current still glows in proportion." },
